Author: lane <lane@local>
Date:   Fri Aug 28 11:18:15 2026 +0800

    t-sort: SORT BY/GET dereference, admitted when one executor owns every shard
    
    Implements the full BY/GET surface (substitution templates, hash-field
    patterns, NULL weights, the conversion error, dontsort per type, the
    set/STORE determinism rule, GET projection incl. '#', STORE of
    projections, SORT_RO) in a new feature file src/cmd/t_sort.cc, and
    refuses the dereferencing forms when more than one executor exists --
    the derived key set is only knowable after the source has been read, so
    it cannot be routed, and executing it across executors would need a
    distributed transaction over a dynamically discovered read set, which
    this tree's script engine already refuses by design.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0131nXyQ5SvYWSgqqkHefHVb

