The 93 residual diffs are an oracle-locale artifact, not a gather defect. No server code changed.

Key findings:

- `so:a_0`–`so:a_99` are initialized once at ops 137–236 and never mutated.
- Every `BY so:a_*` command includes `ALPHA`; the logger’s `o[:4]` hid it.
- Op 279’s target order exactly matches C/byte collation of the actual weights.
- Op 280 is really `SORT so:z1 BY so:a_* ALPHA LIMIT 2 2`. The hidden LIMIT explains its single-element response; locale ordering selects `95` instead of `13`.

Harness fixes:

- Redis now boots with `LC_ALL=C` in [differ_gate.sh](/home/user/Projects/tomokv-cpp-sortxshard/tests/differ_gate.sh:161).
- The SORT suite preflights actual collation on both servers and fails clearly when mismatched in [differ.py](/home/user/Projects/tomokv-cpp-sortxshard/tests/differ.py:5539).
- SORT diagnostics now print the full argv in [differ.py](/home/user/Projects/tomokv-cpp-sortxshard/tests/differ.py:5712).
- Full reconstruction and gather audit recorded in [NOTES-SORTXSHARD.md](/home/user/Projects/tomokv-cpp-sortxshard/NOTES-SORTXSHARD.md:156).

Committed:

- `a9b8c7312 test: reject non-C SORT oracle collation`
- `70e50e3d5 docs: explain residual SORT collation diffs`

