The 93 residual diffs are an oracle-locale artifact, not a gather defect. No server code changed.

Key findings:

- `so:a_0`–`so:a_99` are initialized once at ops 137–236 and never mutated.
- Every `BY so:a_*` command includes `ALPHA`; the logger’s `o[:4]` hid it.
- Op 279’s target order exactly matches C/byte collation of the actual weights.
- Op 280 is really `SORT so:z1 BY so:a_* ALPHA LIMIT 2 2`. The hidden LIMIT explains its single-element response; locale ordering selects `95` instead of `13`.

